---
/**
 * The Sonaru mark - an S that is also a sonar wave.
 *
 * **Construction (rev 5).** Rev 2's construction, unchanged: two tangent circles on a
 * horizontal axis, so the S stays level and the curl stays outward.
 *
 * The one lever is **r2**, the second bowl's radius. Tangency puts its centre at
 * `cx + r1 + r2`, so shrinking r2 pulls the tail *left* and makes it smaller, narrowing
 * the mark from the right. Two earlier attempts to get this moved the wrong thing: rev 3
 * spiralled the terminal inward, and rev 4 tilted the axis, which lifted the tail up
 * rather than drawing it in.
 *
 * **The sonar is concentric with the C and crosses it.** `sonarOffset` is 0 and
 * `sonarRadius` (20) is *larger* than `radius` (12), so the wavefront is a wider arc on
 * the same centre and its inner edge passes through the S's stroke: `minGap` returns
 * **−1.75**. That is paired with `sonarOpacity: 0.34` - at the 0.85 this file shipped with
 * earlier the overlap read as a bar drawn across the mark, and at 0.34 it reads as a wave
 * passing behind it.
 *
 * This paragraph described the opposite until 8.10c - a smaller arc set further left and
 * clearing the C, which is what the mark looked like before the owner supplied the final
 * parameter block on 2026-09-08. It was corrected when `/brand` came to document the
 * construction, because the chapter reads its figures from this file's geometry and could
 * not be right while the file's own header said the reverse.
 *
 * **The viewBox is fitted per variant**, computed from the sampled extents of both paths
 * plus half the stroke. A fixed `0 0 100 100` box clipped the sonar's left edge and the
 * tail's right edge at every size - invisible in isolation, obvious in a row.
 *
 * **Final since 2026-09-08**, when the owner declared it so and supplied the parameter
 * block in `PRESET`. It is exact circular arcs with no optical correction - joins
 * unteased, stroke unmodulated where the curve tightens, terminals uncut - and that is
 * now a description rather than a caveat: declaring the mark final **retired** that list
 * instead of completing it (`design-system.md` §9.5). Do not reopen it as cleanup.
 */

import { PRESET, sPath, sonarPath, fitViewBox } from './mark-geometry';

interface Props {
  /** Rendered size in px. The mark is square. */
  readonly size?: number;
  /** Give it a title to expose it to assistive tech; omit for decorative use. */
  readonly title?: string | undefined;
  readonly class?: string | undefined;
}

const { size = 48, title, class: className } = Astro.props;

const s = sPath(PRESET);
const sonar = sonarPath(PRESET);
const viewBox = fitViewBox(PRESET);
const labelled = title !== undefined;
---

<svg
  class:list={['mark', className]}
  viewBox={viewBox}
  width={size}
  height={size}
  role={labelled ? 'img' : 'presentation'}
  aria-hidden={labelled ? undefined : 'true'}
>
  {labelled && <title>{title}</title>}
  <g fill="none" stroke-linecap="round">
    <path class="sonar" d={sonar} stroke-width={PRESET.sonarStroke} opacity={PRESET.sonarOpacity}
    ></path>
    <path d={s} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width={PRESET.stroke}></path>
  </g>
</svg>

<style>
  .mark {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-white);
    flex: none;
  }

  /*
   * The wave is the coloured element (owner, Gate C rev 13). The brand colour had been on
   * the last letter of the logotype; moving it here puts it on the part of the identity that
   * *means* something - the sonar return - rather than on a single letter. The S stays
   * white and reads as the letter; the wave reads as the signal.
   */
  .sonar {
    stroke: var(--color-plum-300);
  }
</style>
